   "summary": "The study compared the traditional taxonomic composition with a trait-based approach of chironomid communities across a habitat gradient in a subtropical subalpine wetland. It found that functional trait groups of chironomids were more robust and sensitive to habitat changes than taxonomy-based approaches."
